From 65b7ebc50158e2abea78794ea51c987f76b00117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Respect serde(default) and skip_serializing_if in tuple
 struct minItems

When deserializing a tuple struct, serde fills in trailing elements that
are missing from the sequence using their default values, if the field or
the container has `#[serde(default)]`. The generated "deserialize" schema
previously always set `minItems` to the number of elements, so it rejected
input like `["abc"]` that deserializes successfully.

Similarly, when serializing, elements with `skip_serializing_if` may be
omitted, so the "serialize" schema should not count them in `minItems`.

Now `minItems` only counts elements that are always present for the
current contract, and is omitted when that count is zero.

Fixes #536
